Both 0result.sql, 1result.sql and 2result.sql return the same correct customer (“STEPHEN QUALLS”).  
However, 1result.sql is the clearest and most maintainable:  
• It uses well‑named CTEs (monthly, diffs, avg_change) so every intermediate step is explicit.  
• It adds a secondary ORDER BY on customer_id to make the tie‑break deterministic.  
• It avoids unnecessary extra nesting (present in 0result.sql) and over‑quoting (present in 2result.sql).  

Hence 1result.sql is the best choice.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```